# LIBRO – Library Management System

A console-based Library Management System developed in Python using CSV File I/O.

## 📌 Project Description

LIBRO is a menu-driven, console-based library management application developed as part of Assignment 1 for MCA Semester I – Python Programming.

The system allows a librarian to manage book records and library transactions through a simple terminal interface. Book and transaction data is stored in CSV files so that the information remains available after the program is closed.

## ✨ Features

- 🔐 Librarian Login
- 📊 Dashboard with library summary
- ➕ Add Book
- 📚 View All Books
- 🔍 Search Book
- ✏️ Update Book
- 🗑️ Delete Book
- 📖 Issue Book
- ↩️ Return Book
- 📋 Issue History
- 🚪 Logout and Exit
- 💾 Persistent CSV File Storage
- ⚠️ Input Validation and Exception Handling

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python 3
- CSV File Handling
- Python Standard Library
- VS Code
- GitHub

## 🧠 Python Concepts Demonstrated

This project demonstrates:

